          "path": "_m/g/c/p/u/streatham-wp/40-42-and-44-streatham-hill-ge.jpg",
          "filename": "40, 42 and 44 Streatham Hill - geograph.org.uk - 1777207.jpg",
          "caption": "40, 42 and 44 Streatham Hill A cluster of three early C19th survivals - some achievement on this road - villas in the Gothick style. The addition of the 'k' denotes the fact that the style is only superficial, being employed to keep up with the latest fashion. Scratch a Gothick building and (usually) a Classical one is revealed. Here, not much scratching is needed, the nod to Gothic being the pointed window tracery. Grade II listed.",
          "alt": "40, 42 and 44 Streatham Hill A cluster of three early C19th survivals - some achievement on this road - villas in the Gothick style. The addition of the 'k' denotes the fact that the style is only superficial, being employed to keep up with the latest fashion. Scratch a Gothick building and (usually) a Classical one is revealed. Here, not much scratching is needed, the nod to Gothic being the pointed window tracery. Grade II listed.",
          "width": 640,
          "height": 398,
          "mimeType": "image/jpeg",
          "license": "CC BY-SA 2.0",
          "artist": "Stephen Richards",
          "sourceUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:40,_42_and_44_Streatham_Hill_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1777207.jpg",
